  PR_BODY: build(deps): one integration branch for sixteen pull requests

Sixteen open pull requests were conflicting with each other rather than with
main: nine were DIRTY, and every one of them carried pnpm-lock.yaml,
apps/*/package.json and apps/api/test/assembly/mutation-results.json. Because
the evidence hashes the WHOLE tracked tree, merging any one of them invalidated
the evidence of all the others — measured live today, merging #60 turned #107
DIRTY within the minute. That is a quadratic cost in the number of open pull
requests, not a queue that needs more patience.

So this is one branch carrying all of them, one lockfile resolution instead of
twelve, and one battery instead of sixteen.

WHAT IS CARRIED

  #107        the push race in regenerate-derived-artefacts (force-with-lease)
  #99 #101    action pins, re-verified at the source rather than taken from the
              bot: upload-artifact 043fb46d = tag v7.0.1, setup-python 5fda3b95
              = tag v7.0.0, both matching character for character
  #32 #33 #56 #58 #59 #61 #85 #86 #87 #102 #104 #105
              thirteen dependency bumps, resolved in ONE
              `pnpm install --lockfile-only` (7.6 s)

vitest 4.1.11 closes GHSA-82fw-gwwq-j7x9, the repository's three open dependabot
alerts.

THREE REAL INCOMPATIBILITIES, FOUND LOCALLY IN MINUTES

Batching found these before CI did — each would otherwise have been a separate
red run of fifteen minutes.

1. vitest 4 widened `vi.fn()`'s return type, so `ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>` no
   longer type-checks as callable. Switched to vi.mocked(), the typed accessor
   vitest ships. That surfaced a second thing: Session never declared
   accessToken, though lib/auth/nextauth.ts returns it — production reached it
   by casting the session to Record<string, unknown>. Now declared, so the field
   is checked instead of asserted.

2. lucide-react 1.x removed its brand icons outright: `Github` is gone, not
   renamed (the 1.39 typings export GitBranch, GitFork, GitMerge and no brand
   mark). A generic git glyph would misidentify the provider on a sign-in
   button, so the official mark is inlined.

3. eslint 10 dropped eslintrc entirely. apps/api was already on a flat config;
   apps/web is migrated to one, extending the same next/core-web-vitals preset.
   No rule changed.

ONE BUMP HELD BACK, BY MEASUREMENT

eslint 10 stays in apps/api and is NOT taken in apps/web. eslint-plugin-react,
which the next preset pulls in, is at 7.37.5 — its newest release — and declares
`eslint ^3 || … || ^9.7`. There is no version of it compatible with eslint 10;
running it under 10 throws `contextOrFilename.getFilename is not a function`.
apps/web therefore stays on eslint 9 until that plugin ships support. Twelve
bumps land, one waits: a batch must not fail whole because one member cannot.

ALSO FIXED HERE, FOUND WHILE MEASURING

regenerate-derived-artefacts wedged a run for 31 minutes: its concurrency group
degenerates to the constant `regenerate-derived-` whenever
`github.event.workflow_run.head_branch` is empty, so unrelated branches share one
bucket. Run 34748798617 (09:00:55Z) was still `queued` while a later run of the
same workflow had finished, and the API refuses to cancel it — 409, "Cannot
cancel a workflow run that has not been queued yet". The group now falls back to
`github.run_id`.

MEASURED BEFORE PUSHING — the caller's own steps, in the caller's own order

  tsc --noEmit  apps/api            0 errors
  tsc --noEmit  apps/web            0 errors
  vitest run                        50 tests, 5 files, all passing
  pnpm lint                         2/2, "No ESLint warnings or errors"
  pnpm build                        3/3 successful
  mutation battery, full regen      85 sites, 0 survived, "No surviving mutant"
  --verify-structure                rc 0, 85 source-bound records

Baseline measured separately on a clean clone of main: apps/web tsc reports 0
errors there too, so the zero above is a comparison and not an assertion. That
