## Supersedes

This branch carries the content of, and replaces, these pull requests. Each is
closed only after its change is verified present here — never before.

| PR | Carried as |
|---|---|
| #107 | `force-with-lease` in regenerate-derived-artefacts |
| #99 | `upload-artifact` pin, re-verified at the tag |
| #101 | `setup-python` pin, re-verified at the tag |
| #32 #33 #56 #58 #59 #61 #85 #86 #87 #102 #104 #105 | one lockfile resolution |

GOVERNANCE-CHANGE: two workflow files change. `graph-admission.yml` moves two
action pins forward to SHAs verified against the upstream tags rather than taken
from the proposing bot, which is exactly the reason `.github/workflows/**` is
excluded from the automated-author path (SEC-0039) — a human-authored change is
the intended route for it. `regenerate-derived-artefacts.yml` receives two
narrowing fixes: a push guarded by `--force-with-lease` against an explicitly
measured SHA, which can only refuse where the previous unguarded push would have
succeeded and can never overwrite a concurrent writer; and a concurrency group
that falls back to `github.run_id` when the branch name is empty, which gives a
context-less event its own bucket instead of wedging the shared one. Neither
grants the workflow any capability it did not already have.

